# Copy to the machine only (never commit real values).
# Paths below match the drawcode box layout; override if yours differ.

# CODEG_TOKEN lives ONLY as a file mode 600:
#   openssl rand -hex 16 > /workspace/codeg-data/CODEG_TOKEN
#   chmod 600 /workspace/codeg-data/CODEG_TOKEN

# Optional overrides used by boot scripts:
# CODEG_DATA_DIR=/workspace/codeg-data
# CODEG_STATIC_DIR=/workspace/codeg-dist/web
# CODEG_MCP_BIN=/workspace/codeg-dist/codeg-mcp
# CF_CONFIG=/home/box/.cloudflared/config.yml   # default: /home/box, then $HOME, then /etc/cloudflared
# PI_ACP_PI_COMMAND=$HOME/.local/bin/pi

# --- Watchdog local config (parsed, never sourced) ---
# codeg-watchdog.sh reads a machine-local copy of this file on every loop:
#   cp deploy/codeg-boot/env.example /workspace/codeg-boot/local.env
#   (or point CODEG_WATCHDOG_CONFIG at another path)
# Only the KEY=VALUE lines below are honoured; other keys in the copy are
# ignored, and nothing is evaluated. Non-empty launcher env overrides the file.
# Edits take effect on the next watchdog loop (~60s); no restart needed.
# Keep the real local.env out of git: it holds this machine's hostname.
#
# Public edge probe: empty/unset means public=unconfigured in watchdog.log
# (with an hourly warning) and 530/1033 zombie tunnels are NOT auto-restarted.
# CODEG_PUBLIC_URL=https://example.com/
# Public recovery restarts cloudflared only, never codeg-server.
# PUBLIC_FAIL_THRESHOLD=2           # consecutive failures; 1..1000
# TUNNEL_RESTART_COOLDOWN=180        # minimum attempt spacing; 1..86400 seconds
# TUNNEL_RESTART_BACKOFF_CAP=1800    # doubles up to this cap; 1..86400 seconds
# TUNNEL_RESTART_DAILY_CAP=0         # 0 disables cap; otherwise 1..1000 per UTC day
# TUNNEL_RESTART_GRACE=60            # after successful force launch; 0..3600 seconds
